# A counted loop that reads the code units of a text made flat in front of it: its turns are laid out in a row ONCE FOR EACH WIDTH: narrow texts take the first row, wide ones the second, and the
# width is asked in front of the rows. Before, a wide text ran the loop as written, which asks the width at every unit: 10.01 instructions a unit against 3.52 (hash), 18.71 against 12.72 (a loop that leaves its turns).
# f1 = hash: never leaves its turns: two rows. f2 = rests: leaves its turns at a comma and comes back: two rows in one ring.
# RUN(EVENT): compile UnrolledLoopsEmitted UnrolledLoopsWithReentry UnrolledLoopsWithSharedReentry mechanisms=all
